IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er6-nouns`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), SCHEDULE I: the regions "for the purposes of Parts I and VIII of the Act".
-- Text: the plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (SOR-96-332.txt, lines 1758-1926);
-- an unofficial conversion, not verified against the official text.
--
-- WHAT THE SCHEDULE DOES. It does not say which region a person is in. It says what each region consists of, in terms of
-- Statistics Canada's census divisions and subdivisions, metropolitan areas and agglomerations. Each region is therefore a
-- rule over a PLACE (er6-nouns): `Regs Sch I s 2(1.2) the place is in the region of Central Ontario` is TRUE when the place
-- consists of what s 2(1.2) lists. The heading over each section names the province: "Census Division No. 11" is a different division in
-- every province, so each rule tests the province first (that test is the heading's, not the subsection's).
-- Where a region is defined as what is left of a division after another region took its part (Huron, s 2(12): "not part of
-- ... the region of Niagara"), the rule calls the other region's rule.
-- Which region applies to a claimant, and its rate of unemployment, is reg 17 (piece er1), not this Schedule: that provision
-- takes the region as an input. The Schedule's title lists the regulations that read it (17(1)(a) and (b), 17.1(1), 18(1),
-- 77.2(2)(b), 77.7(2), 77.8(2), 77.92(2)(a), 77.93(2), 77.94(2), 77.95(2) and 77.97(2)); those are other pieces' provisions.
--
-- ABBREVIATIONS in rule names, as the Schedule's own s 1 defines the full terms: CD is Census Division, CSD is Census
-- Subdivision, CMA is Census Metropolitan Area, CA is Census Agglomeration.
--
-- Repealed in this text, so no rule: s 2(16) ("[Repealed, SOR/2000-268, s. 2]", source line 1807) and s 4(4) and (5)
-- ("[Repealed, SOR/2000-268, s. 4]", source line 1841).

§ `Schedule I s 1 -- interpretation`

DECLARE `er6 Edition of the Standard Geographical Classification` IS ONE OF
    `er6 SGC 1996`
    `er6 SGC 2011`

-- src:1761 | 1 The definitions in this section apply in this Schedule.
-- src:1762 | Census Agglomeration for the purposes of sections 2, 5, 7 and 9, means a census agglomeration within the meaning of the Statistics Canada document entitled Standard Geographical Classification (SGC) 1996 and for the purposes of sections 8, 12 and 13, means a census agglomeration within the meaning of the Statistics Canada document entitled Standard Geographical Classification (SGC) 2011. (agglomération de recensement)
-- src:1763 | Census Division means a census division within the meaning of the Statistics Canada document entitled Standard Geographical Classification (SGC) 1996. (division de recensement)
-- src:1764 | Census Metropolitan Area means a census metropolitan area within the meaning of the Statistics Canada document entitled Standard Geographical Classification (SGC) 1996. (région métropolitaine de recensement)
-- src:1765 | Census Subdivision for the purposes of sections 5 and 11, means a census subdivision within the meaning of the Statistics Canada document entitled Standard Geographical Classification (SGC) 1996 and for the purposes of sections 8 and 12 to 14, means a census subdivision within the meaning of the Statistics Canada document entitled Standard Geographical Classification (SGC) 2011. (subdivision de recensement)
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule I s 1 (src:1761-1765)
GIVEN section IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `er6 Edition of the Standard Geographical Classification`
DECIDE `Regs Sch I s 1 the edition that defines Census Agglomeration in section` IS
    BRANCH IF elem section (LIST 2, 5, 7, 9) THEN JUST `er6 SGC 1996`
           IF elem section (LIST 8, 12, 13) THEN JUST `er6 SGC 2011`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule I s 1 "Census Division" (src:1763)
`Regs Sch I s 1 the edition that defines Census Division` MEANS `er6 SGC 1996`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule I s 1 "Census Metropolitan Area" (src:1764)
`Regs Sch I s 1 the edition that defines Census Metropolitan Area` MEANS `er6 SGC 1996`

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule I s 1 "Census Subdivision" (src:1765)
GIVEN section IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `er6 Edition of the Standard Geographical Classification`
DECIDE `Regs Sch I s 1 the edition that defines Census Subdivision in section` IS
    BRANCH IF elem section (LIST 5, 11) THEN JUST `er6 SGC 1996`
           IF elem section (LIST 8, 12, 13, 14) THEN JUST `er6 SGC 2011`
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Schedule I -- helpers that read the places in the Schedule's words`

-- The Schedule writes "Census Division Nos. 12 to 16, 41, 42, 44 and 46"; this builds the numbers from 12 to 16.
-- src:1776 | (d) Census Division Nos. 12 to 16, 41, 42, 44 and 46.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule I s 2(1.2)(d) (src:1776)
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`Regs Sch I whole numbers from` n `to` m MEANS
    IF n GREATER THAN m THEN EMPTY ELSE n FOLLOWED BY `Regs Sch I whole numbers from` (n PLUS 1) `to` m

-- src:1769 | Ontario
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule I, the heading over s 2 (src:1769)
GIVEN place IS A `er6 Place`
      province IS AN `er6 Province or territory`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch I place in province` IF place's `province or territory` EQUALS province

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule I s 1 "Census Division" (src:1763)
GIVEN place IS A `er6 Place`
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch I place in CD No.` IF place's `census division` EQUALS n

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule I s 1 "Census Division" (src:1763)
GIVEN place IS A `er6 Place`
      ns IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch I place in CD Nos.` IF elem (place's `census division`) ns

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule I s 1 "Census Subdivision" (src:1765)
GIVEN place IS A `er6 Place`
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch I place in CSD No.` IF place's `census subdivision` EQUALS n

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule I s 1 "Census Subdivision" (src:1765)
GIVEN place IS A `er6 Place`
      ns IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch I place in CSD Nos.` IF elem (place's `census subdivision`) ns

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule I s 1 "Census Metropolitan Area" (src:1764)
GIVEN place IS A `er6 Place`
      cma IS AN `er6 Census Metropolitan Area or none`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch I place in CMA` IF place's `census metropolitan area` EQUALS cma

@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule I s 1 "Census Agglomeration" (src:1762)
GIVEN place IS A `er6 Place`
      ca IS AN `er6 Census Agglomeration or none`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch I place in CA` IF place's `census agglomeration` EQUALS ca

§ `Schedule I ss 2 to 14 -- what each region consists of`

-- src:1770 | 2 (1) The region of Ottawa, consisting of the portion of the Census Metropolitan Area of Ottawa — Hull that lies in the Province of Ontario.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule I s 2(1) (src:1770)
GIVEN place IS A `er6 Place`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch I s 2(1) the place is in the region of Ottawa` IF
        `Regs Sch I place in province` place `er6 Ontario`
    AND `Regs Sch I place in CMA` place `er6 Ottawa — Hull CMA`

-- src:1771 | (1.1) The region of Kingston, consisting of the Census Agglomeration of Kingston.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule I s 2(1.1) (src:1771)
GIVEN place IS A `er6 Place`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch I s 2(1.1) the place is in the region of Kingston` IF
        `Regs Sch I place in province` place `er6 Ontario`
    AND `Regs Sch I place in CA` place `er6 Kingston CA`

-- src:1772 | (1.2) The region of Central Ontario, consisting of
-- src:1773 | (a) the portion of Census Division No. 11 that is not part of the Census Agglomeration of Kingston;
-- src:1774 | (b) the portion of Census Division No. 18 that is not part of the Census Metropolitan Area of Oshawa or the Census Metropolitan Area of Toronto;
-- src:1775 | (c) the portion of Census Division No. 43 that is not part of the Census Metropolitan Area of Toronto; and
-- src:1776 | (d) Census Division Nos. 12 to 16, 41, 42, 44 and 46.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule I s 2(1.2) (src:1772-1776)
GIVEN place IS A `er6 Place`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch I s 2(1.2) the place is in the region of Central Ontario` IF
        `Regs Sch I place in province` place `er6 Ontario`
    AND (   (`Regs Sch I place in CD No.` place 11 AND NOT (`Regs Sch I place in CA` place `er6 Kingston CA`))   -- (a)
         OR (`Regs Sch I place in CD No.` place 18
                  AND NOT ((`Regs Sch I place in CMA` place `er6 Oshawa CMA` OR `Regs Sch I place in CMA` place `er6 Toronto CMA`)))   -- (b)
         OR (`Regs Sch I place in CD No.` place 43 AND NOT (`Regs Sch I place in CMA` place `er6 Toronto CMA`))   -- (c)
         OR `Regs Sch I place in CD Nos.` place (append (`Regs Sch I whole numbers from` 12 `to` 16) (LIST 41, 42, 44, 46)))   -- (d)

-- src:1777 | (2) The region of Eastern Ontario, consisting of
-- src:1778 | (a) those portions of Census Division Nos. 2 and 7 that are not part of the Census Metropolitan Area of Ottawa — Hull;
-- src:1779 | (b) the portion of Census Division No. 10 that is not part of the Census Agglomeration of Kingston; and
-- src:1780 | (c) Census Division Nos. 1, 9 and 47.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule I s 2(2) (src:1777-1780)
GIVEN place IS A `er6 Place`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch I s 2(2) the place is in the region of Eastern Ontario` IF
        `Regs Sch I place in province` place `er6 Ontario`
    AND (   (`Regs Sch I place in CD Nos.` place (LIST 2, 7)
                  AND NOT (`Regs Sch I place in CMA` place `er6 Ottawa — Hull CMA`))   -- (a)
         OR (`Regs Sch I place in CD No.` place 10 AND NOT (`Regs Sch I place in CA` place `er6 Kingston CA`))   -- (b)
         OR `Regs Sch I place in CD Nos.` place (LIST 1, 9, 47))   -- (c)

-- src:1781 | (3) The region of Northern Ontario, consisting of
-- src:1782 | (a) those portions of Census Division Nos. 52 and 53 that are not part of the Census Metropolitan Area of Sudbury;
-- src:1783 | (b) the portion of Census Division No. 58 that is not part of the Census Metropolitan Area of Thunder Bay; and
-- src:1784 | (c) Census Division Nos. 48, 49, 51, 54, 56, 57, 59 and 60.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule I s 2(3) (src:1781-1784)
GIVEN place IS A `er6 Place`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Regs Sch I s 2(3) the place is in the region of Northern Ontario` IF
        `Regs Sch I place in province` place `er6 Ontario`
    AND (   (`Regs Sch I place in CD Nos.` place (LIST 52, 53) AND NOT (`Regs Sch I place in CMA` place `er6 Sudbury CMA`))   -- (a)
         OR (`Regs Sch I place in CD No.` place 58 AND NOT (`Regs Sch I place in CMA` place `er6 Thunder Bay CMA`))   -- (b)
         OR `Regs Sch I place in CD Nos.` place (LIST 48, 49, 51, 54, 56, 57, 59, 60))   -- (c)

-- src:1785 | (4) The region of Oshawa, consisting of the Census Metropolitan Area of Oshawa.
