§ `Schedule I -- the region a place is in`

-- The Schedule does not say which of its regions a place is in as a whole: it says what each region
-- consists of. This rule only reads the regions in the order the Schedule lists them and returns the first
-- that holds; the tests assert that no place is in two. NOTHING means no region of ss 2 to 14 consists of
-- the place (the place is outside Canada, or the data is wrong): the text does not answer.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations Schedule I ss 2 to 14 (src:1770-1925)
GIVEN place IS A `er6 Place`
GIVETH A MAYBE `er6 Region`
DECIDE `Regs Sch I the region that the place is in` IS
    BRANCH IF `Regs Sch I s 2(1) the place is in the region of Ottawa` place THEN JUST `er6 the region of Ottawa`
           IF `Regs Sch I s 2(1.1) the place is in the region of Kingston` place THEN JUST `er6 the region of Kingston`
           IF `Regs Sch I s 2(1.2) the place is in the region of Central Ontario` place THEN JUST `er6 the region of Central Ontario`
